course: dictionary
lesson: 15816
title: Unconditional: without any ifs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unconditional is made of un- (meaning not) and condition (a rule that says "only if"). So unconditional means there are no ifs and no limits. «My dog gives me unconditional love: he is happy to see me even when I am grumpy.» The words even when tell you the love does not change, whatever you do.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The enemy had to accept an unconditional surrender, so they gave up completely and made no deal.» Surrender means giving up, and no deal tells you nothing was agreed in return. Try your meaning in the sentence: without any conditions still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Unconditional can also describe a promise or an offer. «She got an unconditional offer from the university, so her exam results did not matter.» An offer like this does not depend on anything else, so the clue is did not matter.
fact: Unconditional means without any conditions or limits; it is complete and does not depend on anything.
fact: Unconditional love is love that does not change whatever you do.
fact: An unconditional surrender means giving up completely, with no deal.
fact: An unconditional offer, such as from a university, does not depend on exam results.
fact: The opposite of unconditional is conditional, which means it depends on something.
exercise: «My dog gives me unconditional love: he is happy to see me even when I am grumpy.» What does unconditional love mean? | Love that only lasts on sunny days | *Love that does not change, whatever you do | Love you have to earn with good marks | Love that is shouted loudly
exercise: «The enemy had to accept an unconditional surrender, with no deal at all.» What does unconditional surrender mean? | Stopping for a short rest | Asking for a deal before giving up | *Giving up completely, with no conditions | Winning a game with a big prize
exercise: «Her offer was unconditional, so she did not need to pass any test.» Find and copy the word that means does not depend on anything. | *unconditional | offer | pass | test
test: Ella says an unconditional offer from a university means she must get top grades first. Is she right? | Yes, but only if she is lucky | No, an unconditional offer does not depend on results | *Yes, every offer depends on results
test: What is the opposite of unconditional, meaning with an if attached? | *Conditional | Unlimited | Complete | Generous
exam: Which sentence uses unconditional correctly? | The rain was unconditional, so we went to the park | He ran unconditional down the hill | My shoes are unconditional because they are blue | *Mum's love for me is unconditional: it stays the same whatever I do
